  "data_quality_notes": [
    "Score % in the demo transcripts is a scaled cohort score (about 30-52), not a 0-100 percentage, and it does not track the letter grade consistently.",
    "The STUDENT INFORMATION 'Cumulative GPA' of a sheet can differ from the last 'Cumulative GPA' of its SEMESTER SUMMARY block (e.g. CHEN MIC 3.111 vs 3.153); edu_student.cum_gpa uses the STUDENT INFORMATION value, rounded to the two decimals that decimal(3,2) allows.",
    "Only 955 of the 3425 SIS catalogue codes appear in All_Course_Lists, so edu_course.title_en stays empty for the other 2470; conversely 496 codes listed in All_Course_Lists are absent from the SIS export and are not seeded as courses.",
    "Some SIS data cells are Chinese prose (grading_basis, component, school, academic_org) and are stored verbatim, including mixed '已评分'/'Pass/Fail'.",
    "Nested AND/OR prerequisite logic cannot be represented by the group_no model; text such as '(A or B) and (C or D)' is flattened to OR alternatives of the codes inside each split fragment (documented approximation).",
    "Prerequisite text is sometimes qualitative ('Basic knowledge of Python') or uses non-catalogue codes (STA2003, MATH2040, EIE3001): these produce no edges and are listed above instead of broken foreign keys.",
    "Competency scores cover 13 course codes that are not SIS codes: 12 are bracketed spellings such as 'ECO(2011)' that normalise to a real code, and DDA5002 (10 rows) does not exist in the export and is skipped.",
    "Only 3 of the 33 programmes in All_Course_Lists are covered by SDS_major_rules_index.json; the SME programmes (会计学/金融工程/...) have no rule variants, so no curriculum is generated for the SME demo students' majors."
  ]
